# Design Rules — Impeccable + Taste Skill + Awesome Design MD
# Source: pbakaus/impeccable · Leonxlnx/taste-skill · VoltAgent/awesome-design-md
# Applied permanently to every UI change in this project.

## THE SLOP TEST
Before shipping any UI: "Would someone immediately know an AI generated this?" If yes, restart.
Name a specific reference before committing to any design direction.

## ABSOLUTE BANS — never produce these
- Side-stripe / left-border accent cards
- Gradient text (background-clip: text)
- Default glassmorphism without a brand reason
- Hero metric sections ("10M users · 99.9% uptime")
- Three identical feature cards with icon + heading + body
- Tiny uppercase tracked labels (FEATURES, WHY US) on every section
- Numbered section decorators (01 · 02 · 03) as scaffolding
- Bounce / elastic CSS easing (cubic-bezier overshoot)
- Dark glows on dark backgrounds
- Em-dashes (—) in UI copy
- Beige + brass "premium consumer" palette without explicit brief
- Cards nested inside cards
- Text overflow at any breakpoint

## FONT REJECT LIST — never use as display/brand font
Inter · Fraunces · Newsreader · Lora · Crimson · Crimson Pro · Playfair Display
Cormorant · Cormorant Garamond · Syne · IBM Plex Mono · IBM Plex Sans · Space Mono
Space Grotesk · DM Sans · DM Serif Display · Outfit · Plus Jakarta Sans · Instrument Sans

## TYPE RULES
- Body minimum: 16px; never px for font-size
- Hierarchy ratio: ≥1.25× between steps
- Line length: max 65ch (max-width: 65ch)
- Body line-height: 1.5–1.7; headings: 1.1–1.2
- text-wrap: balance on headings
- tabular-nums on all numeric/currency content
- 2–3 font families max
- Semantic token names (--text-body, --text-heading)

## COLOR RULES
- Use OKLCH throughout
- Body text contrast ≥4.5:1 (WCAG AA)
- Never pure black (#000) — always tint neutrals
- Never gray text on colored backgrounds without contrast check
- 60-30-10 visual weight distribution
- Always provide dark mode or explicitly opt out

## SPACING RULES
- Base unit: 4px. All values must be multiples: 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64, 96px
- Semantic tokens (--space-sm, --space-md) — never arbitrary values
- Section padding: 96px; card internal: 24–32px
- Max content width: ~1200px centered
- Never identical spacing everywhere — rhythm needs contrast

## LAYOUT RULES
- Flexbox for 1D; Grid for 2D
- Responsive: grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr))
- Squint test: primary/secondary/grouped must be distinguishable blurred
- Container queries for components; viewport queries for page layout

## MOTION RULES
- Every animation needs semantic purpose — no fade-on-scroll everywhere
- Exponential easing (e.g. cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)); no bounce/elastic
- @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) always required
- Never gate content visibility on a transition

## COMPONENT RULES
- Buttons: min 40×40px touch target; one filled CTA per visual band
- Cards: vary sizes/spans; never nest; 24–32px internal padding
- Inputs: 40px height; 8px radius; visible focus state always
- Never remove keyboard focus ring

## ACCESSIBILITY
- Semantic HTML: nav, main, article, section, button — never div for interactive
- All interactive elements keyboard-navigable
- Never skip heading levels
- ARIA labels on icon-only buttons
- aria-live for dynamic content

## ANTI-SLOP CHECKLIST (before declaring any UI work done)
[ ] No reject-list font as display/brand font
[ ] No gradient text
[ ] No side-stripe cards
[ ] No glassmorphism without brand reason
[ ] No hero metric section
[ ] No three-up identical feature cards
[ ] No repeated uppercase kicker labels
[ ] No numbered section decorators
[ ] No bounce easing
[ ] No em-dash in copy
[ ] No text overflow at 320px
[ ] All spacing is 4pt multiples
[ ] No pure black or untinted neutrals
[ ] Contrast ≥4.5:1 on all body text
[ ] Focus ring visible on all interactive elements
[ ] prefers-reduced-motion handled
[ ] Mobile verified at 375px and 320px
[ ] Touch targets ≥40×40px

## DESIGN.MD STANDARD
New projects: create DESIGN.md with these 9 sections:
1. Visual Theme  2. Color Semantics  3. Typographic Hierarchy  4. Component Styling
5. Layout Principles  6. Depth System  7. Design Constraints
8. Responsive Strategy  9. Agent Prompt Guide
